Taichi Lang is a domain-specific language embedded in Python for
high-performance parallel programming.  Python functions decorated
with @ti.kernel are compiled just in time and run in parallel on the
GPU, which makes it suited to physical simulation, numerical
computation, computer graphics and visual computing.

This package builds the Metal backend (ti.init(arch=ti.metal)) for
the Apple GPU; kernels are compiled to SPIR-V, translated to Metal
Shading Language and compiled at run time.
